Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(approval,forms): one resubmit CTA in one place; stop
 x100 rate corruption on edit

Two defects reported against the resubmit flow after the C4b deploy.

1. "2 nut resubmit 1 duoi 1 tren khong dong bo" (approval-page).
   The flow has two stages and each rendered its own call-to-action:
     stage 1  Approved + gbs_status Rejected -> small orange "Resubmit"
              button injected at the BOTTOM, next to "Check Status"
     stage 2  status "Can sua"                -> "Sua & Submit lai" inside a
              yellow banner at the TOP of the page
   Same flow, same destination (/gbs-so-form-v2?edit=<id>), two labels in two
   places. ec-resubmit-merge-v1 gives stage 1 a #ec-gbs-resubmit-banner at the
   top of #content, styled to match #ec-can-sua-banner and carrying the same
   "Sua & Submit lai" label, so nothing moves on screen as the doc advances.
   Verified live: GBS-SO-2026-08-03-00001 (stage 1) and GBS-SO-2026-07-31-00009
   (stage 2) each render exactly one CTA, both at offsetTop 81.

   The insert path also re-arms the 3s poll. ec-resubmit-repoll-v1 only re-armed
   on the "button already exists" branch, which was unreachable: the insert path
   fell off the end of ensureButton(), so the poll died after the first insert
   and the stale-button case it was meant to fix could still occur in-page.

2. Rate rendered x100 on the edit form (gbs-so-form-v2, gbs-po-form-v2).
   fillRow() wrote the raw number into .item-rate:
       rateI.value = String(item.rate)          // "19687535.45"
   but that input is vi-VN formatted ('.' = thousands, ',' = decimal), and every
   reader of it -- parseClean(), parseRateValue() -- strips '.' as a thousands
   separator. 19687535.45 was therefore read back as 1968753545. On
   GBS-SO-2026-07-31-00009 the form showed a grand total of 1.968.753.545 VND
   against a stored grand_total of 19687535.45.

   ec-edit-rate-vnfmt-v1 formats to vi-VN before filling, using the exact options
   of formatViVN() in ec-gbs-rate-input-fix v2 (grouping + maximumFractionDigits
   20) so no precision is lost. Round-trip checked against parseClean for
   19687535.45 / 12962962.962 / 411957490.6 / 7067320.4 / 1000 / 0.
   Verified live: SO 00009 -> "19.687.535,45", total 19.687.535 VND;
   PO GBS-PO-20260617-12949 -> "1.268.218,98", total 1.268.219 VND (stored
   1268218.98).

All three pages were written to team.ecentric.vn under a sha guard, round-tripped
byte-identical, and every <script> block passes node --check (20 blocks on
approval-page, 29 on each form). The two -v2 form pages are live-only, not
repo-managed; only approval-page ships here, with BASELINE_SHA256 bumped and the
repoll-v1 hash moved into SUPERSEDES_SHA256 in the same commit.

Known, deliberately out of scope (separate decision):
  - readDomRows() in the native-SO path uses parseVN(), which drops decimals
    entirely; broken for any decimal rate today, before and after this change.
  - parseBulkText() splits on ',' and writes a raw number into .item-rate, so
    bulk paste has the same class of defect as fillRow() had.
  - parseClean() is also applied to .item-qty, which is type="number" and uses
    '.' as its decimal separator, so a fractional qty like 1.5 reads as 15.

